        "notes": [
          {
            "id": "scripts/build_system_tier.py:module/_detect_frontend.fn/for@0/for@0/if@0/except@0",
            "verdict": "finding",
            "why": "`except Exception: pass` around reading and parsing a package.json while probing for a frontend framework. A malformed manifest, a permissions error or a bug in the probe all vanish identically and the system tier reports no frontend. A narrow `except (OSError, ValueError)` with a note would make the skip intentional; as written it is a swallow."
          },
          {
            "id": "scripts/build_system_tier.py:module/_scan_calls_edges.fn/for@0/except@0",
            "verdict": "finding",
            "why": "`except Exception: continue` around `open(full).read()` in a file loop. An unreadable file is a legitimate skip, but `Exception` also hides a UnicodeDecodeError on a file the scan should have seen, silently dropping its edges. `except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError)` would name the skip."
          },
          {
            "id": "scripts/trace_run.py:module/_Tracer.class/__call__.fn/except@0",
            "verdict": "intended",
            "why": "`except Exception: pass  # noqa: BLE001 - a tracer must never break the run`. The shape is a real broad swallow and the author meant it: a sys.setprofile hook that raises would abort the traced program (PLAN-M-RUNTIME phase 3). The IR cannot read the comment; this wants a stated allowance on the node, not a verb change."
          }
        ],
        "falsePositives": [],
